<p>I think I&rsquo;m finally ready to start writing here. One of the main things that&rsquo;s been holding me back, is that I really wanted my blog posting to work through Org mode.. I finally figured that out.</p>
<p>Basically I have a <em>&lsquo;blog.org&rsquo;</em> file, just like I have other task lists e.g. <em>&lsquo;work.org&rsquo;</em> and <em>&lsquo;personal.org&rsquo;</em> etc. In this file I can write or capture ideas for posts in Emacs as <em>TODO/DOING/DONE</em> type headings. I press a few key binds when it&rsquo;s finished and it exports to markdown, which is capable of being rendered by Hugo into a static website. Now, I know this may seem like a bit of a process to some, but I&rsquo;m actually much more inclined to write something if it fit&rsquo;s in to my current workflow. I&rsquo;m very much in a <em>&lsquo;all my writing starts in org mode&rsquo;</em> place, then.. using org-export-dispatch, ox-hugo, latex, I can generate a html, pdf, markdown, docx, depending on what is needed as an output. It totally makes sense to me that my website should work in the same way.</p>
<p>Another factor that&rsquo;s stopped me from getting started with this is that overwhelming consideration <em>&lsquo;what to actually write about?&rsquo;</em>. The best thing to do, to get past that is just getting started. I think mostly I&rsquo;m going to make this a home base where I can post anything and not take it too seriously.. It&rsquo;ll be Like social media/status updates, short form mostly, some sharing from other places. I get really quite frustrated with actual social media sites, there&rsquo;s a general feeling of not really belonging, wanting to go off and do my own thing - I think that&rsquo;s what this is for initially.</p>
